{% include "_maths_plume.j2" %}
The height of rise of the smoke plume is taken initially to be the average height internally of the warehouse{% if has_undercroft_any %} (discounting the office undercroft){% endif %}. This is updated at each time step to account for the depth of the smoke layer and corresponding amount of clear air through which the smoke plume rises. It is assumed that the smoke plume rises from the floor.
Table {tab:height{{ k }}} shows the average internal height of each of the units.
